# PvP Arena Clients (Web)

- Laravel REST is the only combat authority. `pvp.battle.changed` is a versioned hint — always rehydrate via GET battle/events.
- Drive attack/defense docks from `allowed_actions` + server `can_use`; never invent recover-skip/basic-strike eligibility.
- Reuse one `PvpRealtimeSession` for lobby + battle; fresh ticket/grant on reconnect. No combat commands over WebSockets.
- Mutations need `expected_version` and a stable Idempotency-Key for the same logical retry. On 409, rehydrate; do not auto-resubmit.
- Refresh, tab hide, and navigation must never abandon/forfeit an active PvP battle (5B.4 owns forfeit/timeout).
- Outcome/XP come from server `outcome` + `rewards` only. Do not hardcode +20/+10 in UI math beyond display of server values.
- Keep `features.pvp` release gating on the backend; clients may preview under auth without bypassing ACL.
- Explicit forfeit requires a confirmation dialog; never POST forfeit from pagehide, unmount, beforeunload, or navigation.
- `action_deadline_at` is display-only; never locally declare timeout/loss from the countdown.
- Show “connection interrupted; reconnecting — turn timer may continue” when WS is down; never say the user forfeited.
